  "description": "Decision 289's far-side hinge probe (phase1.25_pilot-wand item 2.7: whether the infinite ring measures a far tap beyond a hinge of the far island rigidly or unfolded), exploratory: 186 copies of the hinged seam pair, the far-side hinge swept convex and concave from 2 to 30 degrees: across a UV seam, under a 1.5 stretched UV, behind a concave and a flat seam fold, with A bent next to the seam, and A bent twice so own taps lie two faces away; each copy its own 3D piece, mesh box exactly [-256, 256] cm in x and z and [-64, 64] in y; document resolution 512. User0-User7 added as RGB32F (a record whose template capture shows one of them not 32F is void); one fill with the eight channels active, Normal at opacity 1, default projection (read back), sources the authored float32 kernel code at the document size: User0-User2 one-hot the nine classes x mod 3 + 3 (y mod 3) of the texel (column x, row y from the top), User3 the UV ramp R = (x + 0.5)/N, G = (y + 0.5)/N, B = 0.5, User4 and User5 the periodic codes d and e (k/256, one 17 x 13 texel tile each), User6 (d + e)/2 and User7 1 - d. The eight maps at OpenEXR 32f with infinite padding and with passthrough (every covered texel must equal its source bit for bit, or the probe is void), every export step done twice in the session.",
